# Implementation Plan - Live Bus Movement & Telemetry Interpolation Stream in SingleBusMap

This plan details how we will enable continuous real-time movement, smooth Leaflet marker animation, and live coordinate/speed/heading updates for single bus tracking on the Admin Console modal (`SingleBusMap`).

---

## User Requirement Summary
When an admin clicks on any yellow bus registration badge (e.g. `UP78KT1322`):
1. **Live Moving Marker**: As the bus runs, its position marker on the map should smoothly glide forward along its trajectory in real-time.
2. **Dynamic Live Telemetry Stream**: The modal side panel displaying **Speed** (e.g. `59 km/h`), **Heading** (e.g. `334°`), **Coordinates** (e.g. `26.111853, 80.595100`), **Destination Status**, and **Regional District** should continuously update live as the bus moves.
3. **Seamless Telemetry Calibration**: When fresh telemetry packets arrive from the UPSRTC backend, the bus marker position and velocity vector seamlessly re-anchor without jarring jumps.

---

## Technical Design & Architecture

### 1. GPS Trajectory Interpolation Engine (`SingleBusMap.tsx`)
- **Real-Time Physics Model**:
  - When `speed > 0` (e.g., $59\text{ km/h} \approx 16.38\text{ m/s}$), convert speed and heading ($\theta$) into delta coordinates per second:
    $$\Delta \text{lat} = \frac{v \times \Delta t \times \cos(\theta \times \frac{\pi}{180})}{111,320}$$
    $$\Delta \text{lng} = \frac{v \times \Delta t \times \sin(\theta \times \frac{\pi}{180})}{111,320 \times \cos(\text{lat} \times \frac{\pi}{180})}$$
- **Animation Loop (`requestAnimationFrame` / 100ms Interval)**:
  - Continuously update the bus's `liveLat`, `liveLng`, `liveSpeed`, and `liveHeading` state variables.
  - Smoothly update Leaflet marker position (`markerRef.current.setLatLng(...)`) and center map camera with ease animation (`mapRef.current.panTo(..., { animate: true })`).

### 2. Live Panel HUD Enhancements
- **Dynamic Compass Indicator**: Add an animated 360° compass rose that rotates live to match `liveHeading`.
- **Live Speedometer Pulse**: Color-code speed changes (Green for moving $\ge 5\text{ km/h}$, Orange for slow traffic, Red for idling).
- **Coordinate Telemetry Ticker**: High-precision 6-decimal latitude & longitude coordinates updating every 200ms as the bus glides.
- **Pulsing Stream Badge**: Add a green glowing **"● LIVE TELEMETRY STREAM"** badge at the top of the sidebar.

### 3. Backend Active Bus Frequency Sync
- **Backend Sync**: Ensure `allBuses` prop in `apps/admin/src/app/page.tsx` passes updated telemetry array every cycle so real GPS packets seamlessly anchor the physics engine.

